                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There are much better sourceports available than this one. When I got it back in 2015, this was a decent way to play the game back then, but it has been overshadowed by BuildGDX and Raze. I wouldn't buy this version, instead I would recommend getting the free Shadow Warrior Classic on Steam and then using the files for either of those sourceports.\n\nShadow Warrior is so fucking good man. It feels great to play and I'd definitely say it's an expert-level FPS game. Be cautious, use your explosives from a distance and don't forget to quick save. Enemies are lethal and there are plenty of tricks and traps in the levels. The type of thing I easily get addicted to.\n\nAll of the weapons are satisfying to use. I love a good grenade launcher and this might have one of the best ever - the explosion radius is giant and it's just as dangerous to you as it is the enemy. Indirect fire bouncing the grenades off the wall is the best way to use it. The railgun is really fun and the rocket launcher has an epic nuke mode. The katana is useful from the beginning to the end, many of the enemies take one or two hits with it. The Evil Ninja enemy has a dramatic anime death when you slash him, too - they freeze for a moment and slowly slice in half. Hell yes.\n\nI also loved the art direction and level design. The environments look great and they are fun to traverse. I was especially happy that some maps have 4 keys you have to find in order to progress, I love a good keycard hunt. I do think there could have been a little more variation, but I was into it from beginning to end.\n\nLo Wang is the most quotable badass to me out of the characters from this era. Cowabunga! I stick firecracker up your ass! Who-a want-a some Wang? He's loud, laughing and having a fun time playing through the game alongside you. I would definitely hang out with this bro.\n\nI've played this game at least three times by now and it never gets old. Don't skip it when you're going back through all the Build engine games.",
